---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout>
  <main class="project-page">
    <a class="back-link" href={`${base}CG_class/`}>Back to Computer Graphics</a>

    <header class="hero">
      <h1>My Fruit Worth</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Pick all of the fruit growing in your garden.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="preview-card">
      <img src={`${base}myFruitWorth.png`} alt="My Fruit Worth project preview" class="project-image" />
      <div class="project-info">
        <p>
          A short game prototype where the player collects fruit from the garden while practicing
          quick decision-making and visual recognition.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a href="https://maya2234.github.io/myFruitWorth/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="primary-button">
            Play the game
          </a>
          <a href={base} class="secondary-button">Home</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="documentation">
      <h3>Controls &amp; Gameplay</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Movement:</strong> Move forward or backward in the direction you are facing. Rotate using the <strong>Left</strong> and <strong>Right</strong> arrow keys.</li>
        <li><strong>Interaction:</strong> When close enough to a fruit object, press <strong>Spacebar</strong> to pick it up and place it in your basket.</li>
        <li><strong>Restart:</strong> Press <strong>R</strong> to restart the game at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Toggle between 3 different visual styles via radio buttons.</li>
        <li><strong>Winning Condition:</strong> A victory screen appears once all fruits have been collected. You can press <strong>R</strong> to play again.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Technical Overview</h3>
      <p>
        Each object type used in the game (<code>house</code>, <code>bush</code>, <code>fruit</code>) is defined as a set of vertices, edges, and faces constructed from the original vertices.
      </p>
      <p>
        Object instances are created with specific position and scaling parameters, then projected using the <strong>pinhole camera method</strong> (dividing $x$ and $y$ by $z$ to project depth).
      </p>

      <h3>Graphics Pipeline Levels</h3>

      <h4>Level 1</h4>
      <ol>
        <li>Loop through each object instance (skipping any collected fruit).</li>
        <li>Apply positioning, scaling, and vertex projection for each model.</li>
        <li><strong>Depth Sorting:</strong> Sort depths from largest to smallest $z$-value so that geometry furthest from the camera is drawn first (ensuring the smallest $z$ in front of the camera draws last/on top).</li>
        <li><strong>Rendering:</strong> Draw faces using HTML5 Canvas methods: <code>beginPath()</code>, step through face vertices with <code>moveTo()</code>, then finish with <code>closePath()</code> and <code>fill()</code>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h4>Level 2</h4>
      <ol>
        <li>Initialize a grid of $320 \times 200$.</li>
        <li>Loop through all object instances (skipping collected fruit).</li>
        <li>Apply scaling, positioning, and projection to the grid for all vertices, pushing valid points to an array (skipping geometry behind the camera).</li>
        <li>Loop through projected vertices and draw each edge starting at $(u_1, v_1)$, stepping pixel-by-pixel along the X-axis and adding the slope on each increment to color the line.</li>
      </ol>

      <h4>Level 3</h4>
      <ol>
        <li>Initialize the grid and skip collected fruit.</li>
        <li>Apply positioning and scaling to object instances and store projected vertices.</li>
        <li>For each object, loop through visible faces (clipping geometry behind the camera).</li>
        <li><strong>Triangle Rasterization:</strong> Calculate the bounding box for the 3 vertices of each face, then evaluate every pixel using <strong>barycentric coordinates</strong> to fill only pixels contained inside the triangle.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Known Issues &amp; Failures</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Collision Detection:</strong> Object collisions are not fully functional. While collision prevention works when approaching house faces head-on, approaching at an angle (after rotating the camera) allows the player to pass through solid faces.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Future Improvements</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dynamic Day/Night Cycle:</strong> Add a setting sun that acts as a game timer, causing the sky to gradually darken.</li>
        <li><strong>Weather System:</strong> Introduce dynamic weather and clouds.</li>
        <li><strong>Basket UI:</strong> Add a visual basket HUD element that fills up as fruits are collected.</li>
        <li><strong>Social Features:</strong> Implement a daily leaderboard.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .project-page {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    color: #111827;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #1d4ed8;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .hero {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .subtitle {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  .preview-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.4);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  }

  .project-image {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 2px solid #dbeafe;
  }
  
    .project-image:hover{
    border-color: #1d4ed8;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(29, 78, 216, 0.18);
    transform: translateY(-1px);        
  }

  .project-info {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .project-info p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #374151;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: linear-gradient(83.21deg, #3245ff 0%, #bc52ee 100%);
    color: white;
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: #e2e8f0;
    color: #0f172a;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover,
  .back-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.92;
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .documentation {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
    border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.35);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .documentation h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .documentation h3 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .documentation h4 {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .documentation p,
  .documentation li {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #374151;
  }

  .documentation ul,
  .documentation ol {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .documentation li + li {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .documentation code {
    background: #eef2ff;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .preview-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
